# Gatsby files
.cache/
# ⚠️ ROOT-ANCHORED, AND IT HAS TO BE. This was a bare `public`, a Gatsby rule
# that matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — including
# packages/frontend/public, which is Vite's static asset directory and the one
# place a file can be served from the site root.
#
# Nothing in it had ever been committed. `favicon.png` sits there, index.html
# has always linked it, and on a clean checkout — which is what Vercel builds
# from — the directory did not exist, so the deployed site answered 404 for its
# own icon. Anything else put there (og.png, robots.txt) would have vanished
# the same way, silently, since it works perfectly on the machine that made it.
/public

